    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "That's right Jackie, these are biennial elections, so like you said, they take place every two years. Now elections are happening for Congress. Congress is made up of two parts, our chambers, the US Senate and the US House of Representatives. There are 100 senators and 435 representatives. So all 435 seats in the House of Representatives are up for grabs, but senators sit for six-year terms which are staggered, so around one-third of the senators up for reelection every two years. That means this year there are 35 seats up for election. So in the current Congress, women hold just over a quarter of the 535 voting seats, and that's at 27% the highest in US history. During the midterms, people won't just be voted for Congress, there are also a number of local and statewide races, including governors and 36 states. And this is important, as some of these officials will be involved in organizing the presidential elections in two years' time.",
