    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49919.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 77,
    "turn_text": "Jackie, I'd be interested in hearing from Chairman Neil about his views on how he thinks the January 6th Committee is playing as an issue in these elections with the electorate, because most of the people we're talking to are talking about the economy. They're not talking about democracy issues or the findings of the J6 Committee. Do you think, German, is that because people are just being polite and they want to avoid this kind of civil war undercurrent? And so the economy is kind of safe ground for them to talk about. Or is January 6 just not having any real traction on these elections?",
